                <mxCell id="qLabel" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#D0D0D0;" value="08 · OPEN QUESTIONS (PROJECTS 2 TO 6)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="20" width="310" x="1230" y="806" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="qBody" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#EDEDED;" value="&lt;font color=&quot;#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;  How good is searched context, and how much of B's lead was the answer key? &lt;font color=&quot;#C8C8C8&quot;&gt;P2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;  Can a small learned classifier route escalations better than rules plus a prompt? &lt;font color=&quot;#C8C8C8&quot;&gt;P3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;  Which failures come from model size, and which from the prompt or grader? &lt;font color=&quot;#C8C8C8&quot;&gt;P4, P5&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#FFFFFF&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;  Do the numbers hold on a stronger model and real Acme emails? &lt;font color=&quot;#C8C8C8&quot;&gt;P6&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="230" width="310" x="1230" y="836" as="geometry"/>
